Step 11.4 is implemented and verified. Summary:

## New modules (`studio/shared/providers_common/`)

| module | contract | closes |
|---|---|---|
| `errors.py` | §34 — `ProviderError`, `ProviderCancelled`, the 16-code catalog, fixed retryability, the §7 workflow mapping, `as_adapter_error()` | D25 |
| `invocation.py` | §30 — `ProviderInvocation`, `CancellationToken`, `ProgressReporter`, `ProviderLogger`, `ArtifactStager` | D22, D29 |
| `results.py` | §31/§36 — `ProviderResult`, `UnitResult`, `Provenance`, `resolve_ref`, `validate_egress` | D23, D28 |
| `jobs.py` | §33 — one `JobHandle`/`JobStatus`, closed state machine, `terminal_outcome()` | D24 |
| `boundary.py` | §34.4/§35 — `invoke()`, `wrap_exception()`, `Deadline`, `wait_until()` | D26 |
| `legacy.py` | today's dict payloads → the envelope, for diffing in 13.x–15.x | — |
| `fixtures.py` | §46's provider-boundary fixture layer | — |

## Changes to shipped code
- `scheduler.py`: `_failure_payload` stops copying `str(exc)`; non-retryable errors end the attempt loop (D27); `ARTIFACT_MISSING` is basename-only (§36 L8).
- Both visual adapters: `EXECUTION_CANCELLED` → `CANCELLED`, `NODE_TIMEOUT` → `POLL_TIMEOUT` (D35/D36). A cancelled Storyboard/Animator node was recorded `failed`; it is `cancelled` now.
- The two duplicate job-dataclass blocks are deleted; both `base.py` files re-export the shared types.

## Two real defects found by first-time test
Both animator providers read `studio.animator.routes._asset_jobs` — an attribute that module has never had, so every `poll()` and Kie AI `submit()` would have raised `AttributeError`. And all five visual `poll()` bodies counted a scene status `"complete"` that neither domain has ever written. Both corrected onto one shared `status_from_scenes()`.

## Deliberate non-change
`ADAPTER_CACHE_SCHEMA_VERSION` is **not** bumped — no adapter output shape changed, only failure-path error codes, which are never cached. A test proves the invalidation mechanism through the injectable parameter instead.

Verification: 510 backend tests (10 live skips, 161 subtests), 154 frontend tests, clean Vite build, no doc drift. Three guards mutation-checked.

